How many types of packages are there in Java?
There are two types of packages in Java

1. User-defined packages
example:
```java
package com.example.myapp;
public class MyClass {
    // class implementation
}

2. Built-in packages 
example:
java.util, java.io, java.net, etc.

Why Packages are used?
Packages are used in Java in order to prevent naming conflicts, control access, and to organize classes.
They help in modularizing the code and make it easier to maintain and understand.


